📖 What I Learned Today

Today I started learning the basics of Computer Networks.

A Computer Network is a system where multiple computers or devices are connected together to share data, resources, and communication.

🌐 Types of Computer Networks

LAN (Local Area Network)

Covers a small area like a home, school, or office.

Example: Computers connected in a college lab.

MAN (Metropolitan Area Network)

Covers a city or large campus.

WAN (Wide Area Network)

Covers a very large area like countries or continents.

Example: The Internet.

🔑 Basic Components of a Network

Router – Connects different networks.

Switch – Connects multiple devices within the same network.

Modem – Connects a network to the internet.

Cables/Wireless signals – Used for communication.

💡 Why Computer Networks Are Important

File sharing

Internet access

Communication (email, video calls)

Resource sharing (printers, storage)

📚 Conclusion

Computer Networks help devices communicate and share information efficiently. Understanding networking basics is important for fields like cybersecurity, cloud computing, and software development.
